The boundary is whether the outcome **identifies a particular figure or event as the thing being tracked**, with the rest explaining, comparing, qualifying, or showing another side of that same bet. A component of a total or a shortage beside shipment growth can be context under D436. A causal connection alone is not enough: when several independently changeable figures or events are presented without a primary one, neither is main.

The hardest cases are `u2/clean-10` and `u3/clean-10`: both connect capacity with supply conditions, but the former presents capacity and prices as coequal, while the latter identifies an amount and relates timing and shortage relief to it. `u3/clean-11` also tests how much weight to give a parenthetical second split.
